message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Admitted known forcings that remain distinguishable after a stiff–sloppy reduction"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  After a documented stiff-sloppy or MBAM-style reduction that preserves
  multi-channel ranks, which Thesis #19-admitted known forcings stay
  distinguishable from soft-prior leakage into Theta, and which admissions
  become artefacts of the unreduced coordinates? On this synthetic toy the
  product forcing and the pool forcing stay distinguishable on the reduced
  chart. The gain forcing is admitted and is a rescaling of kappa, so it is
  confounded with leakage on both charts. The readout forcing is
  distinguishable only on the channel the reduction deletes. Refusals and
  admissions leave the SHA-256 of Theta unchanged. Not a medical device.
  No document DOI.
keywords:
  - forcing admission
  - evidence gate
  - stiff-sloppy reduction
  - manifold boundary approximation
  - multi-channel identifiability
  - soft prior
  - parameter leakage
  - synthetic toy
  - research-only
